WEBVTT

00:03.795 --> 00:09.926
Of all the many forms of magic,
four stand above the rest.

00:12.387 --> 00:16.641
Nourishing all things
and commanding the source of life.

00:16.725 --> 00:18.101
The Sigil of Water.

00:20.061 --> 00:23.023
Turning stone to sand and sand to stone.

00:23.773 --> 00:25.775
Master of change and motion,

00:25.859 --> 00:27.444
the Sigil of Earth.

00:28.737 --> 00:33.116
Carrying knowledge beyond all bounds,
making the impossible journey possible,

00:33.199 --> 00:34.826
and bringing forth progress.

00:34.909 --> 00:36.327
The Sigil of Levitation.

00:37.829 --> 00:41.583
And serving as the blade
and the shield of the people,

00:43.293 --> 00:44.544
the Sigil of Flame.

00:46.629 --> 00:48.882
These four are known to the witches

00:48.965 --> 00:52.093
as the Primary Tetrad.

00:53.261 --> 00:56.014
Now then, shall we give it a go?

01:16.868 --> 01:19.788
Oh no! What do I do?!

01:24.209 --> 01:26.169
Are you okay?

01:26.252 --> 01:28.463
Thanks, Tetia.

01:28.546 --> 01:30.673
Oh! Thanks for your thanks!

01:30.757 --> 01:33.051
So what were you doing, Coco?

01:33.551 --> 01:37.806
I was drawing a fireball spell
to practice levitation magic.

01:38.848 --> 01:41.267
The Sigil of Flame can be dangerous

01:41.351 --> 01:44.771
since something formless must be
kept at the right size and balance.

01:44.854 --> 01:46.689
Be careful with it.

01:46.773 --> 01:48.316
I'll be careful.

01:52.153 --> 01:55.532
You conquered the Dadah Range
right off the bat,

01:55.615 --> 01:57.909
so why levitation magic now?

01:58.785 --> 02:00.328
You flew like whoosh, right?

02:00.411 --> 02:02.956
Like whoosh, swoosh, zoom!

02:03.957 --> 02:08.628
I ruined the sylph shoes
I borrowed from Agott then.

02:09.170 --> 02:11.589
I wanted to fix them
before I returned them.

02:12.632 --> 02:15.677
All that's left is to redraw the seal,

02:15.760 --> 02:18.429
but my lines come out wobbly.

02:19.848 --> 02:24.102
Maybe your wand wasn't the right fit.

02:24.686 --> 02:28.606
The weight and how it feels
in your hand can really matter.

02:29.107 --> 02:30.859
This is just my old one,

02:31.943 --> 02:35.613
so you might want to try holding some
for yourself to choose.

02:39.075 --> 02:41.536
Come on, Coco!
Let's go to the stationer's!

02:41.619 --> 02:42.787
The stationer's?

02:42.871 --> 02:47.750
Yes, a magical stationery shop where
you can get all kinds of magic tools.

02:47.834 --> 02:49.127
A stationery shop?

02:49.210 --> 02:50.879
Let's go to the stationer's.

02:50.962 --> 02:53.631
A magical stationer's?!

02:53.715 --> 02:55.884
It's like a dream come true!

02:55.967 --> 02:57.635
Hey, Coco?

02:57.719 --> 03:01.181
I'm savoring the moment,
so please give me a second.

04:47.412 --> 04:48.371
AN ENOUNTER IN KALHN

04:48.454 --> 04:50.290
That's Kalhn, a town in the Marshwoods.

04:50.373 --> 04:54.919
That island on the sandbar is
the largest town of witches in our area.

05:05.096 --> 05:06.639
Wait up!

05:06.723 --> 05:08.891
A seal to fluff your skirt...

05:08.975 --> 05:11.394
I finally got my wand
to work with my conjuring ink.

05:11.477 --> 05:13.396
There are so many witches!

05:14.272 --> 05:16.149
This section of the river island

05:16.232 --> 05:20.403
started as a watchtower
built by witches to protect the town

05:20.486 --> 05:23.865
from the molewyrms living in
the Marshwoods across the bank.

05:24.365 --> 05:27.160
Witches gathered here
and it became an atelier district,

05:27.243 --> 05:28.077
and even now...

05:28.161 --> 05:30.121
Master Qifrey, Coco's distracted.

05:30.204 --> 05:31.039
Honestly,

05:31.122 --> 05:33.583
if I tag along sightseeing with Coco,

05:33.666 --> 05:35.293
it'll be a waste of time,

05:35.376 --> 05:38.755
so I'm going on ahead.
There're shops I want to see anyway.

05:38.838 --> 05:41.382
Meet us at the stationer's
on the way back.

05:43.343 --> 05:46.179
How are things going with Agott?

05:47.221 --> 05:48.514
If I can,

05:49.015 --> 05:51.517
I'd like for us to be closer.

06:05.323 --> 06:06.824
Hey!

06:07.992 --> 06:09.744
Over here!

06:16.542 --> 06:19.087
This is like a dream...

06:36.896 --> 06:40.817
Coco! We're gonna get separated!

06:46.322 --> 06:48.574
Kalhn is always so crowded!

06:48.658 --> 06:50.827
I'm a little tired.

06:52.036 --> 06:53.746
Here's the stationer's.

06:53.830 --> 06:55.123
The Starry Sword.

07:20.064 --> 07:22.191
There's a tree in the shop.

07:22.692 --> 07:24.026
My, my.

07:24.610 --> 07:29.949
A witch's apprentice
surprised by the silverwood tree?

07:31.909 --> 07:35.163
You don't even know something so basic?

07:35.246 --> 07:36.873
Go easy on her.

07:36.956 --> 07:39.750
Coco's only just become an apprentice.

07:41.752 --> 07:44.172
Then this is the girl?

07:46.340 --> 07:48.885
Well then, no wonder she didn't know!

07:48.968 --> 07:51.721
Ah, my apologies, miss.

07:51.804 --> 07:54.599
I didn't know about you either,

07:54.682 --> 07:55.766
so we're even.

07:58.436 --> 07:59.937
This is Mr. Nolnoa.

08:00.021 --> 08:03.232
He's the owner of this stationer's,
The Starry Sword!

08:03.316 --> 08:04.775
Indeed.

08:04.859 --> 08:09.947
All the components you'll find here were
crafted by me and my grandson, Tartah.

08:10.031 --> 08:14.619
Wands, inks, we've got it all.

08:14.702 --> 08:18.206
You can even extract magic ink
at whatever concentration you like.

08:18.289 --> 08:19.707
Extract?

08:22.919 --> 08:24.128
Coco, was it?

08:24.212 --> 08:26.214
I'll show you. Come along.

08:27.006 --> 08:27.882
Yes!

09:21.060 --> 09:22.144
It turned black!

09:22.645 --> 09:24.272
That is woodcruor.

09:24.355 --> 09:27.441
The branches are silver-white
when healthy,

09:27.525 --> 09:29.777
but turn black when they wither.

09:30.611 --> 09:35.324
It's poisonous to the tree
and to people like this,

09:35.992 --> 09:38.244
but once it's boiled

09:38.327 --> 09:40.830
and drained of excess fluid,

09:42.665 --> 09:48.212
it becomes the source of magic.
Raw conjuring ink.

09:50.172 --> 09:52.883
Ordinary ink is made by collecting soot

09:52.967 --> 09:55.344
from the smoke of burned wood,

09:55.428 --> 09:56.971
but conjuring ink is different.

09:57.054 --> 10:00.391
It's literally made by
taking blood from the tree.

10:01.058 --> 10:03.936
That's why the silverwood tree

10:04.020 --> 10:06.230
is so special to witches.

10:06.314 --> 10:07.857
Indeed.

10:07.940 --> 10:11.235
Strangely,
you can't get it from any other tree.

10:11.319 --> 10:13.029
What an amazing tree.

10:13.112 --> 10:14.280
A very important tree.

10:14.363 --> 10:17.366
Right! There's even an old legend.

10:18.117 --> 10:19.327
That's right.

10:19.410 --> 10:23.706
Long ago, a silverwood tree
fell in love with a witch,

10:23.789 --> 10:25.666
so they say.

10:25.750 --> 10:29.378
It offered its blood as conjuring ink
and its branches as a wand.

10:29.462 --> 10:30.671
Wand!

10:32.173 --> 10:34.925
Did you come to buy a wand?

10:35.009 --> 10:35.843
Yes.

10:43.559 --> 10:44.644
In that case,

10:45.478 --> 10:47.188
to test things out...

10:54.737 --> 10:56.697
I'll give you this.

10:59.367 --> 11:03.037
I'm sure you'll find
a perfect wand for yourself.

11:07.833 --> 11:09.794
What kind would work for you?

11:09.877 --> 11:12.296
I like mine on the lighter side.

11:12.880 --> 11:13.964
What'd be best?

11:19.762 --> 11:21.389
Wait!

11:26.102 --> 11:27.103
Coco!

11:28.312 --> 11:29.939
What should we do?

11:30.022 --> 11:31.023
I don't know.

11:31.107 --> 11:33.776
But Coco will get lost on her own.

11:33.859 --> 11:35.486
Then we have to go after her!

11:46.497 --> 11:48.249
Huh?! What?

11:49.166 --> 11:50.292
Agott!

11:51.001 --> 11:52.211
What's wrong?

11:55.339 --> 11:56.799
You come too, Agott!

11:56.882 --> 11:58.217
Hey, wait...

11:59.802 --> 12:01.178
What's going on?

12:29.498 --> 12:31.500
Coco! Hold up!

12:34.587 --> 12:36.255
Wait, Coco!

12:52.688 --> 12:54.106
What are you doing, Coco?!

12:54.190 --> 12:55.566
Where are you going?

12:55.649 --> 12:59.612
Where? I saw them! The person
who sold me the book on forbidden magic.

12:59.695 --> 13:00.696
That witch!

13:03.282 --> 13:04.450
Huh?

13:04.533 --> 13:06.619
Honestly, always causing a fuss.

13:06.702 --> 13:09.121
But I'm glad we didn't get separated!

13:09.205 --> 13:10.873
Right? Should we head back?

13:10.956 --> 13:11.832
Hey.

13:12.833 --> 13:16.837
We just turned down one alley
and the whole place is different.

13:17.421 --> 13:18.714
Brushbuddy is gone too.

13:19.673 --> 13:21.217
Now that you mention it,

13:21.926 --> 13:24.303
the scenery's totally different.

13:28.098 --> 13:31.519
Kalhn doesn't have white stone walls
and floors like this.

13:33.270 --> 13:34.480
Which means

13:35.064 --> 13:36.732
this isn't Kalhn.

13:38.108 --> 13:39.735
There's no way!

13:39.819 --> 13:43.614
We didn't go through any window-way,
and it's not like we teleported!

13:43.697 --> 13:46.158
I'll go check from the sky!

13:47.827 --> 13:50.079
Tetia may have a point.

13:50.162 --> 13:50.996
What?

13:51.664 --> 13:55.501
We may have been directly teleported
without us realizing.

13:55.584 --> 13:59.713
Huh? But I though magic like that
wasn't allowed.

13:59.797 --> 14:01.382
Because that'd be...

14:01.966 --> 14:02.967
Forbidden magic.

14:04.218 --> 14:07.763
Crap, crap, crap!
We are definitely not in Kalhn!

14:07.847 --> 14:09.181
We have to get out of here!

14:09.265 --> 14:10.516
Hey!

14:10.599 --> 14:12.142
Tetia! What's wrong?

14:12.226 --> 14:15.563
Tetia, calm down.
What exactly did you see?

14:15.646 --> 14:19.233
It's not just that I saw it. It saw me!

14:20.985 --> 14:23.988
I have no business with the others, but...

14:37.793 --> 14:40.004
Welcome, Coco,

14:40.087 --> 14:41.922
to the world of magic.

14:46.343 --> 14:49.972
You are our only hope.

14:51.849 --> 14:52.725
Mr. Nolnoa.

14:53.309 --> 14:55.352
Have you seen my apprentices?

14:55.936 --> 14:59.231
Oh? Did they get bored and go for a walk?

14:59.315 --> 15:00.733
Bored? Of course not!

15:00.816 --> 15:03.068
There is no shop more fun than this!

15:03.152 --> 15:04.695
I can spend all day looking!

15:04.778 --> 15:06.989
Cut it out. You're making me blush.

15:07.698 --> 15:09.950
Besides, they're not the type of girls

15:10.034 --> 15:12.620
who would leave without thanking you.

15:12.703 --> 15:14.163
Where could they have gone?

15:14.663 --> 15:16.248
I was watching, but

15:17.082 --> 15:20.502
they ran after a witch
dressed kinda funny.

15:21.086 --> 15:24.423
Some kind of eyeball-looking mask.

15:36.560 --> 15:37.853
Keep still.

15:38.354 --> 15:39.939
Don't avert your eyes.

15:40.022 --> 15:41.982
Slowly back away.

15:42.691 --> 15:46.236
When we step back,
I'll give a signal, and you run for it.

15:57.706 --> 15:59.041
Steady...

15:59.959 --> 16:01.085
Keep going...

16:07.841 --> 16:08.926
Now!

16:24.566 --> 16:26.235
Now's our chance. Run!

16:34.076 --> 16:37.204
Agott, that spell was amazing!
Was it fire magic?

16:37.287 --> 16:40.165
A flame sigil spell.
An arrow wrapped in wind.

16:40.249 --> 16:42.418
You drew that in that split second?!

16:42.501 --> 16:43.460
Of course not!

16:44.169 --> 16:47.047
If you prep some seals
in your palm quire ahead of time,

16:47.131 --> 16:48.716
you can just close the circle

16:48.799 --> 16:50.551
and activate the spell.

16:50.634 --> 16:53.345
That's amazing, Agott!
You're so cool!

16:53.429 --> 16:55.556
Do you understand the situation we're in?!

16:56.348 --> 16:57.558
Agott!

16:57.641 --> 16:59.977
It's no good. This is a dead end!

17:00.894 --> 17:01.979
Let's find a different way--

17:07.192 --> 17:08.736
What should we do?

17:09.236 --> 17:12.072
The dragon will catch us,
and we'll be eaten!

17:15.367 --> 17:17.119
I don't want to die.

17:18.245 --> 17:21.790
I haven't left a single piece
of magic for the world yet!

17:21.874 --> 17:23.876
How could this have happened?!

17:33.343 --> 17:35.387
Tetia, get a hold of yourself.

17:35.471 --> 17:37.556
We're witch apprentices.

17:38.265 --> 17:40.100
We'll use our magic.

17:41.643 --> 17:42.561
Right.

17:45.189 --> 17:48.150
I'll create a hole
with the wall breaker seal.

17:48.233 --> 17:50.235
Richeh and Tetia, you buy us time.

17:50.319 --> 17:51.904
- Okay.
- Got it.

17:51.987 --> 17:54.656
- Oof.
- Where should I draw it?

17:54.740 --> 17:55.824
Around there.

17:55.908 --> 17:57.326
Add the arrow...

17:57.826 --> 17:59.912
Hey, Agott, come here a sec!

17:59.995 --> 18:00.871
Her eyes

18:01.371 --> 18:04.083
told me she blamed me.

18:04.666 --> 18:07.628
Yes, let's go with that for now.

18:08.128 --> 18:09.129
And

18:09.630 --> 18:10.798
she's right.

18:18.722 --> 18:19.681
Please...

18:22.518 --> 18:23.936
Fly!

18:32.986 --> 18:35.072
That should buy us a little time!

18:35.155 --> 18:36.865
Good work, Tetia.

18:36.949 --> 18:37.783
Nice.

18:38.367 --> 18:40.536
Tetia is incredible.

18:49.044 --> 18:49.878
That's...

18:51.004 --> 18:52.422
Hey, Agott!

18:55.008 --> 18:57.010
Oh, I'm sorry! I...

18:57.886 --> 19:01.181
What were you thinking?!
How could you touch me when I'm drawing!

19:01.265 --> 19:03.183
I'm sorry! I didn't mean to!

19:03.267 --> 19:05.227
Didn't mean to?

19:05.310 --> 19:06.436
Of course not.

19:06.520 --> 19:08.689
Turning your mother to stone,

19:08.772 --> 19:11.358
dragging us into danger...

19:11.441 --> 19:13.694
You're going to say
you didn't mean any of it, right?

19:13.777 --> 19:15.946
It's all your fault, Coco!

19:16.530 --> 19:18.907
You're uninformed and unschooled,

19:18.991 --> 19:20.450
so don't do anything!

19:24.788 --> 19:26.456
What should we do?

19:27.207 --> 19:28.959
There's no time to redraw.

19:29.543 --> 19:31.587
We'll have to find a different path--

19:31.670 --> 19:32.629
It's fine.

19:39.887 --> 19:40.846
There!

19:41.972 --> 19:44.224
Thank goodness. Well done, Richeh.

19:44.308 --> 19:46.685
Let's hurry and get away.

19:50.898 --> 19:52.816
I meant from this place.

19:54.443 --> 19:58.197
You can take it to mean either way though.

20:28.560 --> 20:30.229
Master Qifrey,

20:30.896 --> 20:33.232
what should I do?

20:39.655 --> 20:41.031
Qifrey!

20:41.114 --> 20:43.283
Did you find them?

20:45.452 --> 20:48.664
No. At least not outside...

20:49.498 --> 20:50.666
I didn't expect this.

20:50.749 --> 20:54.294
For the Brimmed Caps
to make direct contact.

20:54.378 --> 20:55.545
Wait!

20:59.216 --> 21:01.301
So that was a Brimmed Cap.

21:01.385 --> 21:04.513
Never thought they'd be here
of all places.

21:06.515 --> 21:10.560
They hide their faces
behind ancient hats and masks.

21:10.644 --> 21:13.230
They're a dangerous group
who use forbidden magic.

21:14.982 --> 21:17.776
I thought Coco might give me
a lead on them,

21:18.360 --> 21:20.821
but I never expected them
to make direct contact.

21:22.864 --> 21:26.910
Tartah, do you remember anything else?
Anything at all?

21:27.869 --> 21:30.205
Um, I'm sorry.

21:30.289 --> 21:31.665
I don't remember much.

21:32.249 --> 21:33.083
I see.

21:34.501 --> 21:35.919
You're...!

21:42.509 --> 21:44.428
You're the brushbuddy Coco brought back.

21:45.012 --> 21:46.763
Were you with the girls?

21:48.348 --> 21:49.433
Know where they went?

21:59.109 --> 22:00.444
The sun will be setting soon.

22:01.820 --> 22:02.946
Please,

22:04.031 --> 22:05.282
let them all be safe.

23:30.575 --> 23:35.956
Subtitle translation by: Emily Noguchi

23:36.665 --> 23:40.961
DRAGON'S MAZE
